    "analysis": "Silver and gold can provide a diversification benefit and hedge against inflation risk. Historically, both precious metals tend to maintain their purchasing power in the face of inflation. The average annual returns of both commodities from 1970 to 2022 are approximately 7.7% and 3.8% for gold and silver, respectively. However, their risk profiles differ, with gold's generally higher volatility and value retention when faced with high inflation. Given the allocation limit of 15%, and assuming equal risk aversion between gold and silver, we can propose an allocation of 50% to each. As the total allocation equals 10%, the rebalancing trigger will not be triggered. Inflation correlation rationales for both gold and silver: both serve as a hedge against inflation since they historically appreciate value when inflation rises.",
